/T (It might be argued that active euthanasia entails several serious and highly questionable implications despite all attempts to prove its feasibility. The main challenge associated with it is related to the likelihood of abuse and coercion. For example, the elderly, individuals with disabilities, and financially struggling persons may experience implicit pressure to opt for active euthanasia because this act would not reflect their actual desires but rather impose their perceived responsibility to ease other people's suffering. This undermines the very principle of voluntary choice that advocates emphasize. )
/E (It might be argued that active euthanasia entails several serious and highly questionable implications despite all attempts to prove its feasibility. The main challenge associated with it is related to the likelihood of abuse and coercion. For example, the elderly, individuals with disabilities, and financially struggling persons may experience implicit pressure to opt for active euthanasia because this act would not reflect their actual desires but rather impose their perceived responsibility to ease other people's suffering. This undermines the very principle of voluntary choice that advocates emphasize. )
