/P 140 0 R
/T (The basic principle behind passive euthanasia is the recognition of the autonomy of the patient. A competent individual has the right to reject any form of treatment, even if their decision could lead to their own death. Decisions regarding patients who cannot make  their own decisions usually depend on their advance directives or living wills, or on the advice of their families and physicians acting in their best interest. )
/E (The basic principle behind passive euthanasia is the recognition of the autonomy of the patient. A competent individual has the right to reject any form of treatment, even if their decision could lead to their own death. Decisions regarding patients who cannot make  their own decisions usually depend on their advance directives or living wills, or on the advice of their families and physicians acting in their best interest. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
