/T (Non-voluntary euthanasia means ending someone's life when they can't consent because they're unconscious, have severe mental limitations, or can't communicate. Usually,  family members, guardians, or doctors make this decision, thinking it's in the patient's  best interest. It's generally used when there's no hope of getting better and the person is enduring lots of suffering, whether that's physical pain or emotional distress. )
