/T (One of the main reasons for controversy is the conflict between the right to life and the right to die. Supporters argue that individuals should have autonomy over their own  bodies and the freedom to choose a dignified death, especially in cases of severe illness. Opponents, however, believe that life is inherently valuable and should be protected  under all circumstances, regardless of suffering. This creates a fundamental ethical disagreement that is difficult to reconcile. )
/E (One of the main reasons for controversy is the conflict between the right to life and the right to die. Supporters argue that individuals should have autonomy over their own  bodies and the freedom to choose a dignified death, especially in cases of severe illness. Opponents, however, believe that life is inherently valuable and should be protected  under all circumstances, regardless of suffering. This creates a fundamental ethical disagreement that is difficult to reconcile. )
