/P 150 0 R
/T (Supporters of euthanasia often challenge the slippery slope argument, stating that strong legal safeguards and oversight can prevent such expansion. However, critics maintain  that no system is immune to change over time, especially when influenced by social, economic, and medical pressures. )
/E (Supporters of euthanasia often challenge the slippery slope argument, stating that strong legal safeguards and oversight can prevent such expansion. However, critics maintain  that no system is immune to change over time, especially when influenced by social, economic, and medical pressures. )
