/T (The ECHR also reflects a balance between state protection of life and individual autonomy. Courts have repeatedly emphasized that protecting vulnerable individuals is a legitimate reason for restricting assisted dying laws. At the same time, they acknowledge that end-of-life decisions involve deeply personal and moral considerations that vary  across societies. )
/E (The ECHR also reflects a balance between state protection of life and individual autonomy. Courts have repeatedly emphasized that protecting vulnerable individuals is a legitimate reason for restricting assisted dying laws. At the same time, they acknowledge that end-of-life decisions involve deeply personal and moral considerations that vary  across societies. )
