/Title (Voluntary euthanasia is the practice in which a mentally competent individual freely and explicitly consents to end their own life to escape unbearable suffering, most commonly caused by a terminal or incurable illness. The key defining element is informed consent, meaning the patient fully understands their medical condition, prognosis, available alternatives, and consequences of the decision, and chooses euthanasia without coercion, pressure, or impaired judgment.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 787 0 R
/Next 791 0 R
>>
endobj
